<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/function/ontology#Function> .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ProjectionFunction> .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "coarsen coordinates to the enclosing region (generalization, P10)"@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Disclosure control by generalization (#72, CONSTITUTION P10): a place that carries gmeow:coarsenTo a target gmeow:GranularityLevel is projected with the coordinates of the enclosing ancestor at that level INSTEAD of its precise point — a coarser region rather than exact coordinates, never deletion. Aligns by reference to dpv:Generalisation. Ancestor SELECTION is performed declaratively in the SPARQL projection (the gmeow:containedInPlace+ path matching the ancestor whose gmeow:hasGranularity is the target level); this transform documents the resulting generalization, receiving the already-selected ancestor's coordinates (paramLatitude/paramLongitude) and re-emitting them as the place's location. Heavier geomasking / k-anonymity stays in the solver layer (P12)."@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/queries/projections/geosparql.rq> .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularity> <https://w3id.org/function/ontology#expects> _:l_https___blackcatinformatics_ca_gmeow_fnCoarsenToGranularity_expects_0 .
