<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularityGeoJson> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "coarsen GeoJSON coordinates to the enclosing region (generalization, P10)"@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnCoarsenToGranularityGeoJson> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Disclosure control by generalization (#72, CONSTITUTION P10): a place that carries gmeow:coarsenTo a target gmeow:GranularityLevel is projected with the coordinates of the enclosing ancestor at that level INSTEAD of its precise GeoJSON — a coarser region rather than exact coordinates, never deletion. Receives the already-selected ancestor's GeoJSON and re-emitting it as the place's location. Heavier geomasking / k-anonymity stays in the solver layer (P12)."@en .
