<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnPronounSetToText> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/function/ontology#Function> .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnPronounSetToText> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ProjectionFunction> .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnPronounSetToText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pronoun set → full five-form declension text"@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnPronounSetToText> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Renders a gmeow:PronounSet's full five-form declension as a single slash-joined string (subject/object/possessive-determiner/possessive/reflexive, e.g. 'she/her/her/hers/herself', 'xe/xem/xyr/xyrs/xemself') for emission as the vCard 4 PRONOUNS property (RFC 9554, free text), carried on the GMEOW-minted vcardx:pronouns extension term because the W3C vCard RDF ontology never minted a predicate for it. Because PRONOUNS is free text it carries the whole declension LOSSLESSLY — no form is dropped, and a consumer can reconstruct the full set. The only non-representable parts are the non-specifying values (pronounAny / pronounAsk / pronounNameOnly, which carry no forms) and any period / standpoint on the assertion."@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/fnPronounSetToText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/queries/projections/vcard.rq> .
